Instead of an interface, you can use a class to generate a dynamic set of user profile objects on-the-fly. This allows you to easily add new properties or methods without needing a type-safe interface.

```typescript
class UserProfile {
  constructor(public name: string, public email: string) {}
  addProperty(key: string, value: any) {
    this[key] = value;
  }
}
```

This way, you can build userProfile objects with any number of properties on demand, making your code very flexible and adaptable.

